                <pb facs="1097" n="1017" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg1017"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Eddy to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-12-26"><hi rendition="#italic">December 26,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Eddy reports favorable news from Messrs. Gargiulo and Peet, the committee
                    sent to Djumabala, stating that they are in close touch with brigands and will
                    leave Salonica on December 27 for an unknown point on the frontier, where a
                    meeting with the most of the leading brigands will take place. Mr. Eddy has
                    every hope of their success.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
